-- M4 (spec §10): constructor payloads via docassemble `show if`.
--
-- `enum-triage.l4` is the nullary case, shipped at M1: an `IS ONE OF` whose
-- constructors carry nothing rides as one `datatype: radio` question and the
-- `CONSIDER` arms compile to `==` comparisons. This file is the case M1
-- refused by name: constructors that CARRY something.
--
-- The idiom here is the one the corpus actually uses — the escape hatch
-- (`refused HAS the stated reason IS A STRING`) and the qualified grant
-- (`granted subject to conditions HAS the number of conditions IS A NUMBER`).
-- Each payload becomes a FOLLOW-UP question gated on the radio answer, and
-- the gate must be docassemble's `show if:` in its `{code: …}` spelling:
--
--   * the `{variable:, is:}` spelling is browser-side JavaScript only
--     (parse.py:3998-4002 at 1b6678384 sets show_if_var/show_if_val and no
--     showif_code), so the engine shows every field and an API/headless drive
--     DEFINES them all — it cannot encode a constructor payload at all;
--   * the `{code: …}` spelling is evaluated server-side (parse.py:6316-6325
--     evals showif_code and sets extras['ok'][n] = False at 6320/6324), and a
--     field it hides is left genuinely UNDEFINED — not '', not 0, not None.
--
-- Hence the two claims this file exists to test:
--
--   * the follow-up for the constructor that was NOT chosen is never asked;
--   * and it never leaks a default into the computation — on the `granted`
--     path a zero `number of conditions` must not be able to decide the
--     `GREATER THAN 3` test, because on that path the test is not reached at
--     all.
--
-- One hazard is baked into the shape: a `show if: {code: …}` that reads a
-- variable set by a field in the SAME question is fatal (`DASourceError:
-- Infinite loop: <var> already looked for`). The radio must therefore be its
-- own, earlier question — probed against 1.10.7.

DECLARE `Licensing Outcome` IS ONE OF
    granted
    `granted subject to conditions`
        HAS `the number of conditions` IS A NUMBER
    refused
        HAS `the stated ground of refusal` IS A STRING

DECLARE Decision
    HAS
      @desc What the licensing authority decided
      `the outcome` IS A `Licensing Outcome`

@export Whether an appeal lies against the licensing decision
GIVEN d IS A Decision @desc The licensing decision under challenge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies` d IF
    CONSIDER d's `the outcome`
    WHEN granted                        THEN FALSE
    WHEN `granted subject to conditions` n THEN n GREATER THAN 3
    WHEN refused                       g THEN NOT (g EQUALS "non-payment of the fee")

-- An unconditional grant: nothing to appeal. Neither payload question may be
-- asked on this path.
#EVAL `an appeal lies` (Decision WITH `the outcome` IS granted)
-- FALSE

-- A grant on two conditions: within the tolerance, so no appeal. The NUMBER
-- payload is asked; the STRING payload is not.
#EVAL `an appeal lies` (Decision WITH `the outcome` IS `granted subject to conditions` OF 2)
-- FALSE

-- A grant on nine conditions: appealable.
#EVAL `an appeal lies` (Decision WITH `the outcome` IS `granted subject to conditions` OF 9)
-- TRUE

-- Refused for non-payment: pay and re-apply, no appeal. The STRING payload is
-- asked; the NUMBER payload is not — and must not arrive as 0, because a 0
-- that reached `GREATER THAN 3` would be answering a question the law never
-- put.
#EVAL `an appeal lies` (Decision WITH `the outcome` IS refused OF "non-payment of the fee")
-- FALSE

-- Refused on the merits: appealable.
#EVAL `an appeal lies` (Decision WITH `the outcome` IS refused OF "the premises are unsuitable")
-- TRUE
